body:
Work is underway on a new use for eggs for the production of encrypted live images, with the presence of user data.
LUKS technology has been chosen in order to be able to encrypt the entire file system.

* `love` the following flags have been added:
   * `--cryptedclone`, abbreviated as `-k`;
   * `--clone`, abbreviated as `-c`;
* `produce`: the --cryptedclone option now produces an entirely encrypted filesystem named `filesystem.encripted` and located in the `/live` directory of the ISO image. The following lags have also been changed:
   *  the `--kernel` flag now has the uppercase abbreviation `-K`.
   * the `--cryptedclone` flag has the lowercase abbreviation `-k`.
* removed commands `syncfrom`  and `syncto` not more necessaries;
